---
description: Packages under internal/ return errors; only cmd/ decides exit codes
globs: internal/**/*.go
alwaysApply: false
---

Code in `internal/` must never terminate the process. Do not call `os.Exit`, `log.Fatal`, `log.Fatalf`, `log.Panic` or `panic` for expected failures (bad config, I/O errors, HTTP errors, invalid input). Return an `error` instead and let `cmd/jevrules` map it to an exit code (0 ok, 1 findings, 2 usage/config, 3 JEV unavailable).

`panic` is acceptable only for programmer errors that cannot happen at runtime, such as an impossible `switch` default.
